## State Definition

Use `TypedDict` with `Annotated` reducers. Every list field needs an append reducer.

```python
from typing import TypedDict, Annotated
from langgraph.graph.message import add_messages
from langchain_core.messages import BaseMessage

class SignalAnalysisState(TypedDict):
    signal_id: str
    raw_text: str
    company_id: str
    facts: Annotated[list[dict], lambda a, b: a + b]
    sentiment: str
    confidence_score: float
    summary: str
    error: str | None
    messages: Annotated[list[BaseMessage], add_messages]
```

### Reducer Selection

| Pattern | Reducer | Use Case |
|---------|---------|----------|
| Replace value | No reducer needed (last-write-wins) | `sentiment`, `confidence_score`, `error` |
| Append list | `lambda a, b: a + b` | `facts`, `patterns`, `signal_texts` |
| Messages | `add_messages` | Chat history (built-in dedup + ordering) |

