## ToolNode from langgraph.prebuilt

Use `ToolNode` for explicit tool execution loops. Never handle tool calls inside model nodes.

```python
from langgraph.prebuilt import ToolNode
from langchain_openai import ChatOpenAI

tools = [search_tool, scrape_tool]
llm = ChatOpenAI(model="gpt-4o").bind_tools(tools)

async def model_node(state: SignalAnalysisState) -> dict:
    response = await llm.ainvoke(state["messages"])
    return {"messages": [response]}

tool_node = ToolNode(tools)

graph.add_node("model", model_node)
graph.add_node("tools", tool_node)
graph.add_conditional_edges("model", should_call_tools, {
    "tools": "tools",
    "end": END,
})
graph.add_edge("tools", "model")  # loop back to model after tool execution
```

### ToolNode Rules

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Explicit loop | Model → conditional → ToolNode → model |
| Never hide tool calls | Graph must see every tool invocation |
| Bind tools to LLM | `llm.bind_tools([tools])` before model node |
| Tool-loop guard | Add iteration counter to prevent infinite loops |

